  "equipment_type": "Thermostat (BACnet MS/TP)",
  "applies_to": "Strato OS214 / OS214W room thermostats running the fan coil (2-pipe / 4-pipe) application of the universal firmware.",
  "summary": "In its fan coil unit (FCU) application the OS214 drives a valve (BO-1 or AO-1) and a three-speed fan (BO-2 to BO-4) over BACnet MS/TP. The object list gives setpoints, mode, fan mode and occupancy commands, changeover and fan status, demands and two PID loops. It shares 38 object IDs with the RTU list but many objects differ.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Universal firmware 1.0.4 and later",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "The guide has no read/write column. Access here follows its tags: Cfg, User and Cmd objects are shown writable, Status objects read-only, and BO/AO objects commandable (the guide lists them for output overrides).",
    "AI-2 is printed in the I/O table without a row border and was read from the page text.",
    "Multistate state numbers follow the order the states are printed, starting at 1.",
    "MSV-62, MSV-65 and MSV-77 print a value range instead of a state list."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "OS214x (Universal Firmware) User Guide, Fan Coil Unit (FCU) - BACnet Objects",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "Sept 2025 rev 5",
